###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The surface-energy MAE is printed as '0.032 eV/A'; surface energies are energies per area, so the unit is left out of mlips:hasUnit. CHGNet and M3GNet surface-energy MAEs are shown only in Fig. 2(a).
# - Softening scales (force slopes) and corrected MAEs (cMAE) are not accuracy metrics of the schema; the cMAEs (0.184, 0.162, 0.155 eV/A) are not encoded.
# - Whether the Li2B3PO8 high-energy states of Fig. 5(a) are the same configurations as the 100 fine-tuning test structures is implied ('originate from the same set of atomic arrangements') but not stated as identical sets.
# - The DFT functional is not named beyond the MPRelaxSet settings.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/deng2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

